  <body>
    <header class="shell nav"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="mark">7</span><span>IGOR VEPRETSKI / 7YA</span></a><nav class="links" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/">Home</a><a aria-current="page" href="/igor-vepretski/">Igor</a><a href="/journey/">History</a><a href="/evidence/">Evidence</a><a href="/starton/">StartOn</a><a href="/talk/">Talk</a></nav></header>
    <main class="shell">
      <section class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">Official public identity · founder first</span><h1><span class="shine">Igor</span><br />Vepretski.</h1><p class="lead"><strong>Igor Vepretski is the person at the center of 7YA.IO.</strong> An Israeli founder, public-service veteran, creator, and systems builder whose path connects immigration, military and police service, municipal responsibility, youth impact, media, and evidence-first technology.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/journey/">Read the full public history →</a><a class="button secondary" href="/evidence/">Open Evidence</a><a class="button secondary" href="/talk/">Start a serious conversation</a></div></div><aside class="profile"><small>Identity root</small><h2>Igor Vepretski</h2><p>The name, biography, projects, and accountable public record are the primary layer. 7YA is the system around them.</p><div class="rows"><div class="row"><span>Roots</span><b>Kharkiv → Israel</b></div><div class="row"><span>Education</span><b>Criminology</b></div><div class="row"><span>Service</span><b>IDF · Security · Police</b></div><div class="row"><span>Impact</span><b>StartOn</b></div><div class="row"><span>System</span><b>7YA.IO</b></div></div></aside></section>
      <p class="statement"><strong>Founder visibility rule:</strong> every major route should make it immediately clear who Igor Vepretski is, what he has built, which claims are public, and where the complete historical context can be inspected.</p>
      <section class="section"><span class="label">PUBLIC PROFILE</span><h2>One person. Multiple operating chapters.</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="k">Roots</span><h3>Immigrant formation.</h3><p>Born in Kharkiv and raised in Israel after immigrating as a child, with formative years in Bat Yam and Holon.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="k">Service</span><h3>Responsibility under pressure.</h3><p>IDF reconnaissance, security work, an overseas diplomatic-security environment, and Israel Police intelligence and investigation.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="k">Public leadership</span><h3>Municipal execution.</h3><p>Security and beach-supervision leadership in Herzliya, connecting policy, teams, residents, and frontline operations.</p></article><article class="card wide"><span class="k">Social impact</span><h3>Founder of StartOn.</h3><p>A technology-centered model for youth at risk, designed around learning, gaming, mentoring, social support, media creation, community, and practical opportunity.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="k">Creator</span><h3>Signal with purpose.</h3><p>Video, social media, interviews, commentary, music, and storytelling used to route attention toward context and action.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="k">Systems builder</span><h3>7YA.IO.</h3><p>An owned public layer for identity, evidence, media, civic intelligence, social impact, and direct next steps.</p></article></div></section>
      <section class="section"><span class="label">HISTORY AT A GLANCE</span><h2>The public timeline.</h2><div class="timeline"><article class="milestone"><b>1990</b><strong>Kharkiv</strong><p>Birth and Ukrainian roots.</p></article><article class="milestone"><b>1993+</b><strong>Israel</strong><p>Immigration, Bat Yam, Holon, and integration.</p></article><article class="milestone"><b>Education</b><strong>Criminology</strong><p>Study at the Hebrew University of Jerusalem.</p></article><article class="milestone"><b>IDF</b><strong>Palsar 401</strong><p>Armored reconnaissance service.</p></article><article class="milestone"><b>Security</b><strong>Miami chapter</strong><p>International diplomatic-security environment.</p></article><article class="milestone"><b>2015–2021</b><strong>Israel Police</strong><p>Tel Aviv District intelligence and investigation.</p></article><article class="milestone"><b>2023–2025</b><strong>Herzliya</strong><p>Municipal security and beach-supervision leadership.</p></article><article class="milestone"><b>Now</b><strong>StartOn + 7YA</strong><p>Youth impact and evidence-first public systems.</p></article></div></section>
      <section class="history"><div><h2>The complete public story now has a permanent route.</h2><p>The history page expands every chapter while keeping children, private family material, finances, health information, addresses, and sensitive operational details outside the public layer.</p></div><a class="button" href="/journey/">Open Public History →</a></section>
